    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0531" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/951</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Van Dyke</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 31, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 1, 12.10 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>230. Your 134, 29th.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d399-f1"/> Oversea Trust for present
                    prefers not accept non-contraband. Exceptions only possible in special cases for
                        <pb facs="0532" n="274" xml:id="pg274"/> limited quantities by specific
                    arrangement. Tobacco out of question at present. I renew recommendation of my
                    previous despatches 186<anchor n="1" xml:id="d399-f2"/> and 201.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Van Dyke</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
